			"options": {
				"code": {
					"language": "plaintext",
					"showLineNumbers": false,
					"showMiniMap": false
				},
				"content": "<style>\n  @font-face {font-family: 'Quicksand';src: url(\"public/fonts/Quicksand.woff2\") format('woff2')}\n</style>\n<div style=\"color:#548343; font-weight:bold; background-color:#b8bb62;\">\n  &nbsp;TVOCs levels and potential health problems\n</div>\n<div style=\"color:#548343;\">\n  An overview of all pilot sensor devices involved in continuous monitoring grouped by scenario types. Includes bibliographic reference information for interpretation of the totalized values and allows the comparison of situations in different scenarios, in search of patterns or correlations.<br>\n  The 5 stages or so-called IAQ levels extend from Level 1 (excellent) to Level 5 (unhealthy).\n  Extended exposure to increased IAQ levels, i.e., to bad air, can affect the comfort, well-being, and health of building occupants. Poor indoor air quality is linked, e.g., to sick building syndrome, reduced productivity, and impaired learning in schools.<br>\n  Note the following <i>thresholds:</i><br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#50f0e6;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&le;70 ppb</b>: Excellent<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#50ccaa;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>70-200 ppb</b>: Healthy<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#f0e641;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>200-1000 ppb</b>: Unhealthy<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#ff5050;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>1000-5000 ppb</b>: Danger<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#7d2181;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&GreaterEqual;5000 ppb</b>: Hazardous<br>\n  <span style=\"color:#fbcb09;\">More info:</span>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/345329\" target=\"_blank\">World Health Organization (WHO) air quality guidelines (AQGs)</a></li>\n    </ul>\n</div>",
				"mode": "html"
			},
			"pluginVersion": "10.4.3",
			"targets": [
				{
					"datasource": {
						"type": "influxdb",
						"uid": "aqdr-ts-db-flux"
					},
					"query": "from(bucket: \"AIR_QUALITY\")\r\n  |> range(start: v.timeRangeStart, stop:v.timeRangeStop)\r\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._measurement == \"CONTINUOUS_MONITORING_\")\r\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r.AQ == \"IAQ\")\r\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._field == \"co2\")\r\n  |> group(columns: [\"scenario\"], mode:\"by\")\r\n  |> mean()",
					"refId": "A"
				}
			],
			"transparent": true,
			"type": "text"
		},
