				"content": "<style>\n  @font-face {font-family: 'Quicksand';src: url(\"public/fonts/Quicksand.woff2\") format('woff2')}\n</style>\n<div style=\"color:#548343; font-weight:bold; background-color:#b8bb62;\">\n  &nbsp;PM2.5 levels and potential health problems\n</div>\n<div style=\"color:#548343; font-weight:normal;\">\n  PM2.5 is used when describing pollutant levels both outdoor and indoor, where health impact from exposure considers amount of PM2.5 over a 24-hour period. Most studies indicate the following <i>thresholds:</i><br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#50ccaa;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&leq;12 µg/m³</b>: healthy with little to no risk from exposure<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#ff5050;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&gt;35 µg/m³</b>: unhealthy and can cause issues for people with existing breathing issues such as asthma<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#7d2181;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&GreaterEqual;50 µg/m³</b>:  can lead to serious health issues and premature mortality<br>\n  <span style=\"color:#fbcb09;\">More info:</span>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/345329\" target=\"_blank\">World Health Organization (WHO) air quality guidelines (AQGs)</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/figures/mortality-due-to-different-causes\" target=\"_blank\">Mortality due to different causes for PM₂.₅ and NO₂, 2021</a></li>\n      <li><a href=\"https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/analysis/indicators/health-impacts-of-exposure-to\" target=\"_blank\">Premature deaths due to exposure to fine particulate matter in Europe, 2023</a></li>\n      <li>Norway, Poland Recommendations: 40 µg/m³ (8h).</li>\n    </ul>\n</div>",
				"mode": "html"
			},
			"pluginVersion": "10.4.3",
