			"id": 11,
			"options": {
				"code": {
					"language": "plaintext",
					"showLineNumbers": false,
					"showMiniMap": false
				},
				"content": "<style>\n  @font-face {font-family: 'Quicksand';src: url(\"public/fonts/Quicksand.woff2\") format('woff2')}\n</style>\n<div style=\"color:#548343; font-weight:bold; background-color:#b8bb62;\">\n  &nbsp;CO2 levels and potential health problems\n</div>\n<div style=\"color:#548343;\">\n  The levels of CO2 in the air and potential health problems <i>thresholds</i> are:<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#50f0e6;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&leq;400 ppm</b>: typical level found in occupied spaces with good air exchange.<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#50ccaa;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>400-1000 ppm</b>: level associated with complaints of drowsiness and poor air<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#f0e641;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>1000-2000 ppm</b>: level associated with complaints of drowsiness and poor air<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#ff5050;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>2000-5000 ppm</b>: level associated with headaches, sleepiness, and stagnant, stale, stuffy air. Poor concentration, loss of attention, increased heart rate and slight nausea may also be present<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#960032;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&gt;5000 ppm</b>: this indicates unusual air conditions where high levels of other gases could also be present. Toxicity or oxygen deprivation could occur. This is the permissible exposure limit for daily workplace exposures<br>\n  &nbsp;<span style=\\\"font-size:20px;color:#7d2181;\\\">&#9724;</span>&nbsp;<b>&gt;40000 ppm</b>: this level is immediately harmful due to oxygen deprivation<br>\n  <span style=\"color:#fbcb09;\">More info:</span>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/345329\" target=\"_blank\">World Health Organization (WHO) air quality guidelines (AQGs)</a></li>\n    </ul>\n</div>",
				"mode": "html"
			},
			"pluginVersion": "10.4.3",
			"targets": [
				{
					"datasource": {
						"type": "influxdb",
